## Design decisions

- The six checks run on Levels 2 to 4. A review week runs loops-recall and loops-minutes only.
- A part that needs `taught` or `others` and does not get it is named in the label ("not checked: ...").
  When nothing else is wrong, the check reports LOOP_CHECK_STATUS with the detail "not checked: ...". It never passes a skipped part.
  The count rule of loops-recall always runs.
- loops-minutes (Question A, no new rule): only a loop step may carry a loopMinutes that differs from minutes.
  A loop step (not moved) has 2 minutes or more, counted at loopMinutes ?? minutes.
  The day sum is compared with periodMinutes only for a day that holds a changed step (loopMinutes set and different from minutes).
  Reason: the Red Level 3 case (periodMinutes 49) passes only when the days B to E, which have no change, are not summed.
  A day without a changed step keeps the existing `minutes` check. So loops-minutes passes on the shipped weeks w01 to w08.
  This differs from strategy line 216 (six warn per teach week).

